   "reason": "Only sourceHash, tenantSource and the tenant/product controls change on these mutations (multi-tenant #20): mentor_memories is student_global per the classification registry, so the POST and DELETE were keyed by session.studentId without resolveTenantPrincipalContext, serving and mutating a student's mentor memories on any tenant's branded host with no product gate. Each now resolves the acting tenant with strict revocation, confirms the student's binding, refuses a foreign branded host, and runs the Mentor product gate before writing or deleting; a not-available outcome fails closed with 503. The bounded body, CSRF, rate limits and the student_global storage shape are unchanged. Re-pinned because the operation's tenant sourcing moved, verified against the effective manifest and the derived route-guard test.",
